SWAT+ 62.0.1 bug fix, opt in: off unless a run asks for it (routing_fix = "muskingum_daily" in
the TOML config, which starts SWAT+ with --routing-fix=muskingum_daily), so by default the
exchange build routes exactly as stock. Muskingum routing (rte_cha 1) on a daily step:
sd_hydsed_init.f90 splits the day into the substeps the Muskingum stability limit needs and
computes c1, c2 and c3 for one substep, but ch_rtmusk.f90 resets the substeps to 1 on every
call when time%step is 1, so each day is one step with substep coefficients. They go to a
fixed point (c1 0.375, c2 0.625 with msk_x 0.2) whatever K: every reach delays about 0.63 day,
whatever its length, slope or roughness. With the fix, the reset is skipped for rte_cha 1, and:
- sd_channel_control3.f90 sets the day's inflow hydrograph to ht1 on any daily step, not only
  when nsteps is 1. command.f90 builds tsin from the HRUs' total flow plus their lateral and
  tile flow again, so with the substeps kept lateral and tile flow would come in twice;
- ch_rtmusk.f90's inflow is set to 0 for a substep with no inflow; it was the saved value
  from the last channel routed;
- the inflow rate for the rating curve is the substep's volume over the substep's length,
  not over a day.
rte_cha 0 and sub-daily steps are untouched. To be removed once SWAT+ fixes it upstream.
docs/upstream-issue-muskingum-daily.md; tests/test_routing_fix.py.

